<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sa Caleta</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sa Caleta is the site of a Phoenician settlement on the south coast of Ibiza, occupied in the 7th century BCE and abandoned around 600 BCE, when its people probably moved to the site of the city of Ibiza. Its excavated houses, streets and workshops are among the best-preserved Phoenician remains in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> and form part of the Ibiza <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sa-caleta.jpg" alt="Sa Caleta" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: stavros1 · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IB64_The_Cove_of_Sa_Caleta,_28_May_2012.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
